{"name":"Gathering Place","hex":"#ad9466","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gathering place","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A place where people are able to congregate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gathering_place"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gathering Place (Tulsa park)","blocks":[{"text":"Gathering Place is a 66.5 acres (26.9 ha) park along the Arkansas River in Tulsa, Oklahoma. Created by the George Kaiser Family Foundation, and designed by landscape architect Michael Van Valkenburgh, the park was established September 8, 2018. It is open to the public free of charge. At $465 million, Gathering Place is the largest private gift to a community park in U.S. history."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/The_Gathering_place.png/330px-The_Gathering_place.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gathering_Place_(Tulsa_park)","wikidata":"Q60746077"},{"title":"Gathering place","blocks":[{"text":"A gathering place is any place where people are able to congregate. Gathering places may be public; for example, city streets, town squares, and parks; or private; for example, churches, coffee shops, stadiums, and theaters."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Schnorr_von_Carolsfeld_Bibel_in_Bildern_1860_029.png/330px-Schnorr_von_Carolsfeld_Bibel_in_Bildern_1860_029.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gathering_place","wikidata":"Q5527376"}],"images":[],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"The Gathering Place - 32608325518","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/The_Gathering_Place_-_32608325518.jpg/500px-The_Gathering_Place_-_32608325518.jpg","ratio":1.4998446722584653,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Gathering_Place_-_32608325518.jpg","share":0.24125},{"title":"Gathering Place -